<title>SWEDEN: AssiDoman's Sepap sells unit to Norsk Skog.</title>
<headline>AssiDoman's Sepap sells unit to Norsk Skog.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group AssiDoman said on Monday that its partially owned Czech unit Sepap has agreed to sell a newsprint plant to Norwegian forestry group Norske Skogsindustrier AS.</p>
<p>It said the plant, Roto a.s., had an annual capacity of 100,000 tonnes and a turnover of 350 million crowns.</p>
<p>AssiDoman owns 39 percent of Sepap.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
